● exp116: We have exp111's improved sample_label_step logic. Now the init uses the old _is_organic. Memory says asymmetry matters. But I realize the current init calls _is_organic so y0=benign for "organic" outputs.
  The issue may be subtle: the init defaults to MALICIOUS if intent doesn't contain "organic"/"contribution" — which means unknown intents are malicious. That's probably WHY the init → malicious logic helps while
  label_step → benign default helps.

  Let me verify we have both in the current code: YES. Init: benign if _is_organic else malicious. Label_step: malicious if _is_malicious else benign. For common cases (exact intent match), both behave the same. For
  weird outputs, they differ — init says malicious, label_step says benign. This asymmetry is why unifying (exp113) hurt.

  exp116: Try putting content last in the init prompt too (currently has "Based on the community context" after content).

